G5384.def:
φίλος, -η, -ον 
[in LXX chiefly for רֵעַ, אָהַב ;] 
__1. pass., beloved, dear (Hom., Eur., al.). 
__2. Act., loving, friendly (in cl. less frequently and only in poets): Actes 19:31. As subst., a friend; 
__(a) masc., ὁ φ.: Luc 7:6 11:5 14:10 15:6 16:9 21:16 23:12, Actes 27:3, 3Jn.14; opposite to δοῦλος, Jean 15:15; φ. ἀναγκαῖοι, Actes 10:24; with genitive subj., Matthieu 11:19, Luc 7:34 11:6, 8 12:4 14:12 15:29, Jean 11:11 15:13-14; ὁ φ. τοῦ νυμφίου, Jean 3:29; τ. Καίσαρος (see Deiss., BS 167; LAE, 382 f.), Jean 19:12; θεοῦ (see Hort, in l), Jacques 2:23; with genitive of thing(s), τ, κόσμου, Jacques 4:4; 
__(b) fem., ἡ φ., Luc 15:9,†
